OBSERVATION (pre-existing, NOT introduced by U14, not grounds for FAIL):
`TestHandleDeleteAllDataRemoveError` (unmodified by this task's diff — git
diff HEAD on handlers_test.go touches only the three tests around line
493-547 to add expected_count, plus new tests appended after) exercises a
scenario where the guard passes (expected_count matches actual) but the
subsequent os.Remove calls fail (directory chmod 0555). I reproduced this
directly: HandleDeleteAllData returns HTTP 200 "Deleted 0 files" even though
0 of the expected 1 CSV was actually removed. The body text is honest (it
says 0, and a page refresh re-derives CSVCount from disk so no stale state
persists), but a 200 on total remove-failure is a pre-existing gap in the
delete LOOP's error handling, untouched by U14's guard logic (which lives
entirely before that loop). Flagging for the backlog; not a defect in the
expected_count guard this task was scoped to build, and not exploitable to
delete the wrong things or bypass the count check.

